{"Title":"An Act authorizing the county of Nantucket to convey School Street situated in the town and county of Nantucket for purposes of conveyance to the town of Nantucket","BillNumber":"S2942","DocketNumber":"SD3402","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2024-09-05T14:02:55.343"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2024-09-05T14:02:55.3433333"},{"Id":"DAF1","Name":"Dylan A. Fernandes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DAF1","ResponseDate":"2024-09-05T14:02:55.36"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2942/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Cyr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2942) of Julian Cyr and Dylan A. Fernandes (by vote of the town) to authorize the county of Nantucket to convey School Street situated in the town and county of Nantucket for purposes of conveyance to the town of Nantucket.  Municipalities and Regional Government.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.  The county of Nantucket is hereby authorized to convey School Street, as shown on a plan of land entitled “Plan of Taking for Nantucket County Commissioners School Street in Nantucket (Surfside) MA.,” dated May 26, 1981, prepared by John J. Shugrue, Inc., recorded with Nantucket County Registry of Deeds in Plan Book 12-C-1, owned by the county of Nantucket to the town of Nantucket for purposes of conveyance.\r\n\tAny such disposition shall be on such terms and conditions as the Select Board deem appropriate, which may include the reservation of restrictions and easements, all as shown on a map on file with the office of the town clerk.\r\n\tSECTION 2.  The provisions of Chapter 30B of the Massachusetts General Laws and any rights of first refusal in the Commonwealth under the provisions of Section 14 of Chapter 34 of the Massachusetts General laws shall not be applicable to any conveyance authorized hereunder.\r\n\tSECTION 3.  This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[{"Description":"S2942 -- Nantucket","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=19194&title=S2942%20--%20Nantucket"}],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J10","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J10"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}